          "id": "7a574045-6c3d-3ce6-880e-4beb96d323f3",
          "content": {
            "id": "7a574045-6c3d-3ce6-880e-4beb96d323f3",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "The Week in Numbers: Brand sales to Travis Kelce's marketing boost",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: From a major brand sale to Travis Kelce's marketing boost, this is the Week in Numbers.</p><p>:: The Week in Numbers</p><p>:: $4.6 billion</p><p>$4.6 billion is the price\u00a0Gucci owner Kering has agreed on to sell its beauty business to L'Oreal.</p><p>It's a major shift in strategy by new CEO Luca de Meo in a bid to tackle the luxury group's high debt....</p><p>And to refocus on its core fashion business.</p><p>Under the deal, beauty giant L'Oreal will acquire Kering's fragrance line Creed.</p><p>:: 10%</p><p>:: Intel Corporation\u00a0</p><p>Almost 10% is the amount Intel stocks hiked early Friday after the company beat estimates\u00a0for its Q3 earnings.\u00a0</p><p>Net income came in at $4.1 billion - compared to a $16.6 billion loss the same time last year.</p><p>The silicon giant's shares have hiked 90% this year.\u00a0</p><p>And this marks the first earnings announcement after multibillion-dollar investments from Nvidia and Softbank - as well as an unprecedented U.S. government stake.</p><p>:: 5%</p><p>Around 5% was how much oil prices surged early Thursday.\u00a0</p><p>Markets reacted after the U.S. put sanctions on leading Russian suppliers Rosneft and Lukoil over the Ukraine war.</p><p>One analyst said this means refineries in China and India, both major buyers of Russia's oil, will need to find other suppliers or risk exclusion from the Western banking system.\u00a0</p><p>The U.S. said it was prepared to take further action as it called on Moscow to agree to a ceasefire in Ukraine.</p><p>:: 33%\u00a0</p><p>:: Volvo\u00a0</p><p>Over a third was how much Volvo Cars shares soared on Thursday.</p><p>Investors bought up after the automaker announced it beat Q3 profit forecasts.</p><p>Sweeping cost cuts have delivered faster than expected results.</p><p>That's despite Volvo being one of the European carmakers most exposed to U.S. tariffs.</p><p>:: 20%</p><p>20% is the figure Six Flags shares have climbed by this week as the company faces shareholder pressure.\u00a0</p><p>Activist investor Jana Partners has teamed up with football star Travis Kelce to push the company to improve its marketing and customer experiences after disclosing a 9% stake.</p><p>Kelce is star tight end for the NFL\u2019s Kansas City Chiefs and podcast host who recently got engaged to singer Taylor Swift.\u00a0</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: From a major brand sale to Travis Kelce's marketing boost, this is the Week in Numbers.</p><p>:: The Week in Numbers</p><p>:: $4.6 billion</p><p>$4.6 billion is the price&nbsp;Gucci owner Kering has agreed on to sell its beauty business to L'Oreal.</p><p>It's a major shift in strategy by new CEO Luca de Meo in a bid to tackle the luxury group's high debt....</p><p>And to refocus on its core fashion business.</p><p>Under the deal, beauty giant L'Oreal will acquire Kering's fragrance line Creed.</p><p>:: 10%</p><p>:: Intel Corporation&nbsp;</p><p>Almost 10% is the amount Intel stocks hiked early Friday after the company beat estimates&nbsp;for its Q3 earnings.&nbsp;</p><p>Net income came in at $4.1 billion - compared to a $16.6 billion loss the same time last year.</p><p>The silicon giant's shares have hiked 90% this year.&nbsp;</p><p>And this marks the first earnings announcement after multibillion-dollar investments from Nvidia and Softbank - as well as an unprecedented U.S. government stake.</p><p>:: 5%</p><p>Around 5% was how much oil prices surged early Thursday.&nbsp;</p><p>Markets reacted after the U.S. put sanctions on leading Russian suppliers Rosneft and Lukoil over the Ukraine war.</p><p>One analyst said this means refineries in China and India, both major buyers of Russia's oil, will need to find other suppliers or risk exclusion from the Western banking system.&nbsp;</p><p>The U.S. said it was prepared to take further action as it called on Moscow to agree to a ceasefire in Ukraine.</p><p>:: 33%&nbsp;</p><p>:: Volvo&nbsp;</p><p>Over a third was how much Volvo Cars shares soared on Thursday.</p><p>Investors bought up after the automaker announced it beat Q3 profit forecasts.</p><p>Sweeping cost cuts have delivered faster than expected results.</p><p>That's despite Volvo being one of the European carmakers most exposed to U.S. tariffs.</p><p>:: 20%</p><p>20% is the figure Six Flags shares have climbed by this week as the company faces shareholder pressure.&nbsp;</p><p>Activist investor Jana Partners has teamed up with football star Travis Kelce to push the company to improve its marketing and customer experiences after disclosing a 9% stake.</p><p>Kelce is star tight end for the NFL\u2019s Kansas City Chiefs and podcast host who recently got engaged to singer Taylor Swift.&nbsp;</p></body>",
